Springs' days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","rain":"Palm Springs has gotten drier"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 76\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>76\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 80\u00b0F, and the record is 96\u00b0F (1933). The low of <strong>60\u00b0F</strong> was the 8th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 102 since 1922.","t_rec":"Palm Springs has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Palm Springs' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Palm Springs has set <strong class=\"sig\">no standing record lows at all</strong>, far fewer than the 96 that chance alone would give, and <strong>101 record highs</strong>, close to the 96 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (62). Palm Springs' all-time high is 124\u00b0F, on July 5, 2024.","t_chg":"Palm Springs' days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 87 complete years: Palm Springs' average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.94\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.82 to +1.06), about +9.6\u00b0F since 1923. Palm Springs' average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.14\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.23), about +1.5\u00b0F since 1923.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Palm Springs has gotten drier","p_rain":"Palm Springs' yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.26 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.50 to \u22120.01), about \u22122.6 inches since 1923. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 4.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1943 (18.57 in); the driest, 2002 (0.76 in). Palm Springs almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 16 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}